    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>A mortal scholar Embraced in 1566 after independently rediscovering thaumaturgical secrets the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.jaYCq9rVOh0I9NCN]{Tremere} thought only they possessed, Dr. Mortius is Milwaukee's foremost expert on the mysterious \"null zone\" centered on Marquette University, where Thaumaturgy fails and Auspex and Protean grow strangely potent. He secretly manipulates the feminist occult study group the Church of Isis at Mount Mary College, using its psychically sensitive members as unwitting pawns to search the city for him without personal risk &mdash; a use of mortal dupes most Tremere would consider both beneath the Clan's dignity and a Masquerade risk. Only Mark Decker and Parovich know he operates in the city at all. He is the true author of several forbidden rituals still in use by Milwaukee's Tremere.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Eager for praise and validation. If characters get you talking, you will happily demonstrate obscure and largely useless magical inventions at great length.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: Mesita. Haven: a haunted house near Marquette University (see Haunted House ritual, his own invention). Disciplines as printed: Auspex 5, Dominate 4, Thaumaturgy 5 (capped above to this system's 1-5 scale). Rituals: Communicate With Kindred Sire, Defense of the Sacred Haven, Wake with Evening's Freshness, Deflection of Wooden Doom, Illusion of Perfection, Haunted House (the latter two his own creations).",
    "npcType": "vampire"
